OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F136A1783632451
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}                 G2/10
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURESCNetwork BBC TV Presentation:
OL,4,Cslow to embrace female voices
OL,5,
OL,6,FIn the early days of ITV, Barbara
OL,7,FMandell presented a lunchtime bulletin
OL,8,Fwhich was dropped after a few months.
OL,10,FThen Nan Winton read the BBC News
OL,11,Fbriefly in 1960 but fell victim to the
OL,12,Fprevailing attitudes of the time.
OL,14,FBy the mid-70s, there had been a number
OL,15,Fof women newsreaders outside London but
OL,16,Ffor network employing a woman was still
OL,17,Fseen as a gamble.
OL,19,FAngela initially presented the News on
OL,20,F2 and was tried out on the main BBC One
OL,21,Fbulletins in 1975.
OL,23,APub: 06-Oct-2024Qpppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BRewind CNat Radio FNat Sport
FL,137,120,200,300,0,100
PN,13603
SC,0003
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F136A1783632451
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}                 G3/10
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURESCNetwork BBC TV Presentation:
OL,4,Cslow to embrace female voices
OL,5,
OL,6,FShe succeeded and became a regular BBC
OL,7,FOne newsreader the following year.
OL,9,FIf was not by chance that she presented
OL,10,Fall three bulletins on the day they
OL,11,Fwere relaunched in March 1976.
OL,13,FAll this should be seen in the context
OL,14,Fof the time.
OL,16,FThe Equal Pay Act and the Sex
OL,17,FDiscrimination Act both became law in
OL,18,F1975.
OL,20,FMargaret Thatcher was the Leader of the
OL,21,FOpposition and a woman Prime Minister
OL,22,Fwas a real possibility.
OL,23,APub: 06-Oct-2024Qpppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BRewind CNat Radio FNat Sport
FL,137,120,200,300,0,100
PN,13604
SC,0004
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F136A1783632451
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}                 G4/10
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURESCNetwork BBC TV Presentation:
OL,4,Cslow to embrace female voices
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe idea that a woman could not read
OL,7,Fthe news would simply have looked
OL,8,Fsexist by then even if, undoubtedly,
OL,9,Fthere would have been dinosaurs in the
OL,10,Fnewsroom who did not like the thought.
OL,12,FIt took a long time before a rough
OL,13,Fgender balance was achieved but other
OL,14,Fwomen came through the ranks as
OL,15,Freporters and newsreaders in the years
OL,16,Fthat followed.
OL,18,FWomen were also making their mark in
OL,19,Fother areas of factual broadcasting
OL,20,Faround the same time.
OL,23,APub: 06-Oct-2024Qpppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BRewind CNat Radio FNat Sport
FL,137,120,200,300,0,100
