OL,3,GFEATURESCNetwork BBC TV Presentation:
OL,4,Cslow to embrace female voices
OL,5,
OL,6,FIn 1975 Sue Lawley was the main
OL,7,Fpresenter of the Tonight programme (the
OL,8,Fancestor of Newsnight) before she
OL,9,Freturned to Nationwide.
OL,11,FValerie Singleton also demonstrated
OL,12,Fthat she could leave her Blue Peter
OL,13,Fimage behind on Nationwide and, later,
OL,14,FThe Money Programme although she still
OL,15,Fappeared occasionally on BP on special
OL,16,Foccasions.
OL,18,FMeanwhile Barbara Edwards was also
OL,19,Fmaking history even if she was billed
OL,20,Fin Radio Times as the "weatherman".
OL,23,APub: 06-Oct-2024Qpppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BRewind CNat Radio FNat Sport
FL,137,120,200,300,0,100
PN,13606
SC,0006
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F136A1783632451
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}                 G6/10
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURESCNetwork BBC TV Presentation:
OL,4,Cslow to embrace female voices
OL,5,
OL,6,FSo with all this in mind, it seems
OL,7,Fsurprising in hindsight that it was
OL,8,Fstill unusual to hear women network
OL,9,Fannouncers.
OL,11,FSome were tried out on attachment ` but
OL,12,Fmostly filled the daytime shifts, often
OL,13,Fon BBC Two where they had little to do
OL,14,Fapart from read the Service Information
OL,15,Fbulletin and link into Play School.
OL,17,FReportedly complaints were received
OL,18,Fwhen women were heard on the evening
OL,19,Fshifts:
OL,23,APub: 06-Oct-2024Qpppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BRewind CNat Radio FNat Sport
FL,137,120,200,300,0,100
PN,13607
SC,0007
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F136A1783632451
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}                 G7/10
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURESCNetwork BBC TV Presentation:
OL,4,Cslow to embrace female voices
OL,5,
OL,6,FIt is astounding to think of viewers
OL,7,Fobjecting to a woman announcer yet, by
OL,8,Fimplication, accepting a woman
OL,9,Fnewsreader.
OL,11,FIt would be sad to think of
OL,12,FPresentation listening to such
OL,13,Fcomplaints when, it would seem the news
OL,14,Fand current affairs departments would
OL,15,Fhave dismissed any suggestions that
OL,16,Fwomen were unsuitable for high-profile
OL,17,Froles.
OL,19,FLet's face it ` reading the Nine
OL,20,Fo'Clock News or presenting Nationwide
OL,21,Fwas far more important than continuity
OL,22,Fannouncing.
OL,23,APub: 06-Oct-2024Qpppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BRewind CNat Radio FNat Sport
FL,137,120,200,300,0,100
PN,13608
SC,0008
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F136A1783632451
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}                 G8/10
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURESCNetwork BBC TV Presentation:
OL,4,Cslow to embrace female voices
OL,5,
OL,6,FIt's also strange that network
OL,7,Fpresentation appeared to receive
OL,8,Fcomplaints about female voices which
OL,9,Fweren't simply filed in the bin given
OL,10,Fthe circumstances of the time.
OL,12,FBetween 1976 and 1980, the evening
OL,13,Fnetwork announcer on BBC One was only
OL,14,Fheard in London and the South East on
OL,15,Fweeknights. Many regions though
OL,16,Femployed women with no apparent
OL,17,Fknockback.
OL,19,FYou would also like to imagine that
OL,20,Fwhenever a woman was heard on BBC Two,
OL,21,Fits viewers would have been less
OL,22,Fresistant to change.
OL,23,APub: 06-Oct-2024Qpppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BRewind CNat Radio FNat Sport
FL,137,120,200,300,0,100
PN,13609
SC,0009
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F136A1783632451
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}                 G9/10
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURESCNetwork BBC TV Presentation:
OL,4,Cslow to embrace female voices
OL,5,
OL,6,FIt was only in the mid-80s that women
OL,7,Fannouncers seemed to start being heard
OL,8,Fregularly in the evenings on both
OL,9,Fnetworks. So far as we are aware, there
OL,10,Fwas little or no public comment.
OL,12,FToday a huge variety of voices are
OL,13,Fconsidered suitable for Presentation `
OL,14,Fa strong accent or what some would
OL,15,Fconsider bad diction are not
OL,16,Fnecessarily barriers, in the name of
OL,17,Fdiversity.
OL,23,APub: 06-Oct-2024Qpppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BRewind CNat Radio FNat Sport
FL,137,120,200,300,0,100
PN,13610
SC,0010
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F136A1783632451
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}                G10/10
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURESCNetwork BBC TV Presentation:
OL,4,Cslow to embrace female voices
OL,5,
OL,6,FSo it is worth reflecting on the fact
OL,7,Fthat there were few women announcers on
OL,8,Fthe BBC networks for many years even
OL,9,Fwhile women like Angela Rippon were
OL,10,Fsmashing glass ceilings in much more
OL,11,Fprominent and important roles.
OL,23,APub: 06-Oct-2024Qpppppppppppppppppppppp
